   "properties": {},
   "widgets_values": [
    "## outpaint-continue.json (scaffolding)\n\nOutpaint with a CONTROLLED fill\n\nScaffolding, not a curated flow yet: E18's verdict is MEH, so it lives in `scratch/`.\n\n**Why:** `outpaint.json` lets the node fill the new canvas by edge-clamp (a smear) and then lets\nthe sampler replace it, so a clipped object (half a tree) is re-invented rather than continued.\nHere the canvas is padded BEFORE the flow and the mask marks the new area, so the sampler starts\nfrom a fill that carries structure - and `mask_expand_pixels`/`mask_blend_pixels` become live.\n\n**Prerequisite:** `uv run python scripts/pad_image.py <source> --left 512 --right 512\n--mode mirror --out-dir <ComfyUI>/input/_outpaint`, then set the two LoadImage nodes here to\nthose files (`*_padded_<mode>.png` and `*_mask.png`).\n\n**What E18 measured** (cottage, matched denoise 0.6-0.9, blend 64): the mirror fill lowers the\nseam step ratio to 0.83-0.85 against 0.97 for the edge fill, and walls/ground/foliage continue\nacross the boundary. **Caveat:** a mirrored *building* survives - at denoise 0.75 the cottage\nbecomes a refined second cottage, at 0.60 an unmistakable mirror of the first (the E7b\nkaleidoscope). Mirror is therefore best for self-similar content (trees, sky, ground, water); for\na building-dominated frame prefer `outpaint.json`'s invention, or mask just the object and use\nthe inpaint flow.\n\n---\n*How to run it: story **S5** in `HOWTO.md`  ·  Why it is this way: **E18** in the scenarios' `EXPERIMENTS` logs.*"
   ],
   "color": "#332922",
   "bgcolor": "#593930"
  },
